{"name":"Kindling","hex":"#7a7068","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"kindling","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Small pieces of wood and twigs used to start a fire.","The act by which something is kindled."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Illuminated, lit."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kindling"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fire making","blocks":[{"text":"Fire making, fire lighting or fire craft is the process of artificially starting a fire. It requires completing the fire triangle, usually by heating tinder above its autoignition temperature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/DirkvdM_tinder_box.jpg/330px-DirkvdM_tinder_box.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire_making","wikidata":"Q1192478"},{"title":"Kindling (1915 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Kindling is a 1915 American silent drama film produced and directed by Cecil B. DeMille and starring Charlotte Walker, in her film debut. A print of Kindling exists in the George Eastman Museum film archive. The film is based on a 1911 Broadway play by Charles A. Kenyon which starred Margaret Illington and was produced by her husband Major Bowes, later of radio fame."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Kindling_-_1915_film.jpg/330px-Kindling_-_1915_film.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kindling_(1915_film)","wikidata":"Q3815379"},{"title":"Kindling (2023 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Kindling is a 2023 British drama film written and directed by Connor O'Hara in his feature debut, based on his short film Infinite (2016)."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kindling_(2023_film)","wikidata":"Q119856371"},{"title":"Kindling (sedative–hypnotic withdrawal)","blocks":[{"text":"Kindling due to substance withdrawal is the neurological condition which results from